{
  "id": "gps-sps-maintenance",
  "title": "GPS SPS collaborative maintenance (reduced CSG)",
  "chapter": "Use case 3 — GPS SPS maintenance with humans in the loop",
  "chapterOrder": 3,
  "formalism": "csg",
  "tool": "PRISM-games 3.x",
  "summary": "Reduced teaching version of the GPS game: Environment vs. on-orbit staff (Po) vs. on-ground staff (Pg), arbitrated by a non-player Monitor. Probabilities are generated from the GPS SPS parameters.",
  "description": [
    "Three players act concurrently each round: the Environment (env) tries a hazard — unscheduled interruption, short-term or long-term hard failure, soft failure; the on-orbit staff (o) and the on-ground staff (g) decide whether to take a failure and how to repair it.",
    "Short-term hard failure: only Po can repair it, by switching to a redundant subsystem (success Pbeta). Long-term hard failure: if both teams take the task, the Monitor allocates it with OnGroundPriority. Po switches to a redundant subsystem / sends software commands (success Pbeta, unless the satellite is at end of life, p_eol), then tries to move & replace a redundant satellite (Pbeta). If that fails, the task goes to Pg: check spare (pr_build), build + manufacture, launch (Pn).",
    "Per-round failure probabilities are derived from the MTBFs with p_fail = 1 − e^(−t/MTBF), t being the duration of a round. Change t_round or an MTBF and the whole model is regenerated.",
    "This is a reduced model written for teaching (a few hundred states): it keeps the structure of the full model but not its full detail (24 slots, O&M degradation, costs), so the numbers differ from the full model."
  ],
  "objectives": [
    "Model humans as strategic players, not as failure probabilities.",
    "Isolate the contribution of each team by comparing the coalitions <<env,o>>, <<env,g>>, <<env,o,g>>.",
    "Sweep a human priority (OnGroundPriority) and observe the trade-off."
  ],
  "exercises": [
    "Compare PRO5, PRO6 and PRO7: which team reaches the reliability target first?",
    "Sweep OnGroundPriority from 0 to 1 (PRISM Experiments) and compare <<env,o>> R{\"replace\"} with <<env,g>> R{\"manufacture\"}.",
    "Lower Pbeta to 0.5: how does the load move to the on-ground staff?",
    "Bonus: duplicate OnOrbitStaff into a second on-orbit player and watch the state space grow."
  ],
  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "k",
      "label": "Number of rounds",
      "value": "30",
      "description": "Horizon of the properties (k = 1 … 30)"
    },
    {
      "name": "t_round",
      "label": "Duration of a round",
      "value": "0.5",
      "unit": "years",
      "description": "30 rounds × 0.5 y = 15-year design life",
      "source": "Teaching choice"
    },
    {
      "name": "MTBF_ST",
      "label": "Short-term hard failure MTBF",
      "value": "0.5",
      "unit": "years",
      "description": "Handled by the on-orbit staff only (switch to a redundant subsystem)",
      "source": "GPS SPS Performance Standard"
    },
    {
